===Usage notes===
Often used as an example of an [[overliterary]] word, as in Prolocutor's speech in Robert Landis's ''Liberty's Triumph'' ([https://archive.org/details/libertystriumph00landgoog/page/n181/mode/2up?q=appropinquates VIII.381]) or John Maclaurin's poem ''On Johnson's Dictionary'' ([https://archive.org/details/workslatejohnma00dreggoog/page/n84/mode/2up?q=appropinquates l. 47]). Older uses are usually intransitive, while more modern ones are either transitive or intransitive.

